# Prerequisites
*.d

# Compiled Object files
*.slo
*.lo
*.o
*.obj

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Compiled Dynamic libraries
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Fortran module files
*.mod
*.smod

# Compiled Static libraries
*.lai
*.la
*.a
*.lib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app

# Third-party dependencies ARE in the repository -- vendor/ is no longer listed here.
#
# It used to be, which meant a fresh clone did not build: you had to know to clone Dear ImGui and
# download the GLFW binary distribution into the right two paths first, and nothing said so until
# the compiler failed on a missing header.
#
# The compiled-artifact rules above match by extension at any depth, so they also match the parts
# of vendor/ that are legitimately binary -- GLFW ships prebuilt .lib and .dll rather than source.
# Those have to be re-included by name. This only works because vendor/ itself is not excluded:
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory has been excluded, so an exclude-then-negate
# pair on vendor/ would silently keep the libraries out and leave the link failing.
#
# The leading **/ is load-bearing. A pattern with a slash anywhere but the end is anchored to the
# directory holding this file, and the vendor directory is Sand/vendor rather than ./vendor -- so
# `!vendor/**/*.lib` matches nothing here, keeps glfw3.lib ignored, and produces an unresolved
# external at link time with no hint as to why. (The old `vendor/` rule worked because a trailing
# slash is not "a slash in the middle", so it matched at any depth.)
!**/vendor/**/*.lib
!**/vendor/**/*.dll
!**/vendor/**/*.a
!**/vendor/**/*.so
!**/vendor/**/*.dylib

# Build trees someone may generate inside a vendored source tree.
**/vendor/*/build/
**/vendor/*/out/

# GLM is deliberately not vendored: no source file includes a GLM header or names anything in its
# namespace, and its include-path entries have been removed. Ignored rather than merely absent so a
# stale local copy does not get committed by a `git add vendor`.
**/vendor/glm/

.vs/
*.ipch

# MSBuild intermediates and output. x64/ had 16 log and .tlog files committed by accident, which
# change on every build and conflict on every merge.
x64/
Win32/
*.tlog
*.log
*.ilk
*.pdb
*.idb
*.recipe
*.FileListAbsolute.txt

# Package staging produced by tools/package.ps1
dist/

# Window positions, written by imgui at exit. Local to a machine, and the UI has one-shot startup
# placement that only runs when this file is absent -- committing one pins everyone's layout.
imgui.ini

# CMake build trees. Named rather than globbed as build*/ so a source directory that happens to
# start with "build" is not swallowed.
build/
build-web/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
